Press patch 0001: build the CommandOutput TypedDict from a dict.
Purpose: Python 3.13 removed the keyword form TypedDict("Name", field=type). Press v0.154.1
fails to import press/press/doctype/deploy_candidate/cache_utils.py on Python 3.14 with
"TypeError: TypedDict() got an unexpected keyword argument 'cwd'". The dict form keeps the
same four fields, types and required keys.
Upstream: proposal 1 in backend/docs/press-python314-upstream.md.
Remove when Press ships this change (decision O-51 in backend/PROJECT-RECORD.md).

diff --git a/press/press/doctype/deploy_candidate/cache_utils.py b/press/press/doctype/deploy_candidate/cache_utils.py
index a599d6d..24288f7 100644
--- a/press/press/doctype/deploy_candidate/cache_utils.py
+++ b/press/press/doctype/deploy_candidate/cache_utils.py
@@ -12,10 +12,7 @@ from typing import Tuple, TypedDict
 
 CommandOutput = TypedDict(
 	"CommandOutput",
-	cwd=str,
-	image_tag=str,
-	returncode=int,
-	output=str,
+	{"cwd": str, "image_tag": str, "returncode": int, "output": str},
 )
 
 
